# Persistent Workspaces: Creation and Deduplication

## (1) Persistent Workspaces with "*" Monitor Key

When `persistent-workspaces` uses `"*"`, workspaces are created **once per monitor**, not globally.

The code iterates through each monitor's configuration:

```cpp
const bool monitorInConfig = std::ranges::find(keys, currentMonitor) != keys.end();
for (const std::string &key : keys) {
    bool canCreate = key == currentMonitor || (key == "*" && !monitorInConfig);
```

The wildcard acts as a fallback—it only applies to monitors not explicitly listed. Each monitor processes its own persistent workspace set independently.

## (2) Deduplication by ID/Name

Yes, workspaces are deduplicated. The `createWorkspace()` function prevents recreation:

```cpp
auto workspace = std::ranges::find_if(m_workspaces, [&](std::unique_ptr<Workspace> const &w) {
    if (workspaceId > 0) {
      return w->id() == workspaceId;
    }
    return (workspaceName.starts_with("special:") && workspaceName.substr(8) == w->name()) ||
           workspaceName == w->name();
```

If a workspace with matching ID or name already exists, it updates persistence flags instead of creating a duplicate.

## (3) `all_outputs` Filtering

The `all_outputs` flag determines which workspaces get buttons. During initialization:

```cpp
if ((allOutputs() || m_bar.output->name == workspaceJson["monitor"].asString()) &&
    (!workspaceName.starts_with("special") || showSpecial()) &&
    !isWorkspaceIgnored(workspaceName)) {
      m_workspacesToCreate.emplace_back(workspaceJson, clientsJson);
```

When `all_outputs()` is true, all workspaces qualify regardless of monitor assignment. Otherwise, only workspaces matching the current monitor's name are displayed.

